  "body": "Introduces a new `<poster>` element that brings `<img>` element capabilities to HTML `<video>` poster images, including responsive image selection and accessible description of the poster frame.\n\nBasic example, using resolution switching and an `alt` description of the poster image:\n``` html\n<video src=\"skater.mp4\" poster=\"skater.jpg\">\n  <poster>\n       <img alt=\"A skateboarder slides down a handrail above a concrete staircase.\" \n           srcset=\"skater.jpg 800w, skater-lrg.jpg 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 1200px\">\n  </poster>\n</video>\n```\n\nAnother example using a `picture` element, with inherited lazy loading.\n``` html\n<video src=\"skater.mp4\" loading=\"lazy\">\n  <poster>\n   <picture>\n    <source srcset=\"skater-9x16.avif\" type=\"image/avif\">\n    <img src=\"skater-9x16.jpg\" alt=\"A skateboarder slides down a handrail above a concrete staircase.\">\n   </picture>\n  </poster>\n</video>\n```\n\n[More examples in spec draft](https://whatpr.org/html/12585/media.html#the-poster-element)\n\nFixes  #10378\n\n<hr>\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n\nWhen you submit this PR, and each time you edit this comment (including checking a checkbox through the UI!), PR Preview will run and update it. As such make any edits in one go and only after PR Preview has run.\n\nIf you think your PR is ready to land, please double-check that the build is passing and the checklist is complete before pinging.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Mozilla: [✅](https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1426)\n   * Chromium: [✅ ](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12585#issuecomment-6084062137)\n   * Webkit: [no declared position](https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/689)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * [Web Platform Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62290) authored by [alexgoff](https://github.com/alexgoff) - marked tentative by filename.\n- [x] Browser Implementations/Prototypes\n   * [Chromium](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549635)\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * [Chromium](https://issues.chromium.org/issues/571666824)\n   * [Gecko](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2080232)\n   * [WebKit](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326997)\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs:\n   * [HTML-AAM](https://github.com/w3c/html-aam/issues/618)\n   *  [ARIA-in-HTML](https://github.com/w3c/html-aria/issues/608)\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n   * [MDN Ticket](https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/883)\n- [x] [W3C TAG Design Review Requested]https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1311)\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/embedded-content-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/embedded-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/embedded-content.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/embedded-content.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/image-maps.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/image-maps.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/image-maps.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/images.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/media.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 13, 2026, 3:56 PM UTC (dfa60b5)\">/media.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12585/c18a7c5...dfa60b5/media.html\" title=\"Last updated o